title The stack held the third step -- Tally coverage falls from three gaps to two
prompt Take one bounded DREAM systems-core lap, Lindy-first and crux-first; prove the seam from both sides, distinguish a machine limit from a tree defect, commit path-limited, pull twice, and leave the tree clean.
think The fire rota read at N=3742, row 2: see the bright point directly, hold the stopped line, give the red its allocation, and cut only as deep as the truth asks. The constellation table then pointed to Tally's choir-and-bijection row. Its roster already stood, with three honest gaps under a falling ceiling: kumara, the deprecated pedersen shim, and stack.
think Stack was the crux-first gap. Its test filled two slots and named the third push in prose, yet no owned witness ran the unwelcome side. The new direct witness builds and runs the exact-bound, reverse-order, and empty-value paths; then it plants one more push in a throwaway copy and requires the process to stop at stack.top < max. The first witness run caught its own channel defect: std.debug.print speaks on stderr, while the harness read stdout. Reading pass.err repaired the witness, and both sides then answered on this Linux metal.
obs The cold roster ran 93 guards: 85 green and 8 red. The Caravan suite took about twelve minutes and completed green; that duration is a machine cost on this pier, not a Tally defect. The direct stack ownership gap was a tree defect: the roster credited no check because none existed, and this lap closes it with a two-sided witness. Coverage moves 8 covered and 3 uncovered to 9 covered and 2 uncovered; a newborn without a check still refuses above the ceiling, a longer name still earns no false credit, and the healed pen passes at zero.
obs The other hand was the Sound seat's 20260829.145726 package, pulled from xy before this file moved: one enclosure door, fifteen wire-lab shims, and one almanac engine. Its log arrived without its day-index row, so this lap restores that row beside its own rather than leaving the shelf seam red. Hush's existing stash remains untouched. QA was B or better for every opened artifact at its proper class; MAP first read C+ under my wrong Door setting, then A+ at Meter as the standing pointer-card rule requires.
